Q: Show same image on scroll and animate based scroll A: <p>I strongly recommend <a href="https://greensock.com/scrolltrigger/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">scrollTrigger</a> library by greensock. You can basically recreated the apple scrolling experience by configuring various animations and then deciding which animation plays once you hit a certain viewport height.</p>
<p>Here is a simple example: <a href="https://codepen.io/GreenSock/pen/gOabMXv" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://codepen.io/GreenSock/pen/gOabMXv</a></p>
<p>Code ( by Greensock) below:</p>
<pre><code>gsap.timeline({
  scrollTrigger: {
    trigger: &quot;.shoe&quot;,
    start: &quot;center center&quot;,
    end: &quot;bottom top&quot;,
    scrub: true,
    pin: true
  }
})
  .from(&quot;.midsole&quot;,  { y: innerHeight * 1.5 })
  .from(&quot;.outsole&quot;, { y: innerHeight * 1.5 });
</code></pre>
<p>And here is a link to the docs: <a href="https://greensock.com/docs/v3/Plugins/ScrollTrigger" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://greensock.com/docs/v3/Plugins/ScrollTrigger</a></p>
